ARGUMENT IN FAVOR OF MEASURE “H”
Currently, the city’s Admission Tax Ordinance does not speciﬁcally exempt
those who attend charitable, religious, or political events, or events held
at our hotels, from paying the tax. Measure H ﬁxes that problem.
The city’s Admission Tax is paid by residents and guests who purchase
tickets to events in Indian Wells. It was never intended to apply to those
attending charitable, religious, or political events, or to events held at our
hotels, which is why your City Council unamiously voted to clarify the
issue by placing Measure H on the ballot.
You can read the full text of Measure H in this ballot pamphlet. You
can also learn more about Measure H on the city’s website at www.
indianwells.com.
We urge you to vote yes on Measure H to clarify this issue and support
our local charitable, religious or political organizations and those residents
and guests who purchase tickets to their events.
